&lt;li&gt;Serve as the dedicated partner to our G&amp;amp;A leadership, planning and managing our investments in headcount, real estate, IT and benefits to ensure they are aligned with company strategy and durable growth goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ongoing analysis of business performance vs. plan to highlight trends, identify risks and opportunities, and influence executive decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and summarize our P&amp;amp;L and cash flow narrative for executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up public-ready performance management structures across headcount and expense like monthly budget vs. actuals, re-forecasting, and a recruiting commit process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor a high-performing team (2 P4s, 1 P3)—providing strategic direction, career development support, and hands-on collaboration to drive team impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get a bird’s eye view of Figma’s entire business, shape investments in our next chapter of growth, and build foundational infrastructure for the next decade of strategic finance at Figma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a builder’s mindset to scaling the Corporate Finance function—identifying tools, metrics, and systems that drive automation and enable better decision-making at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of total experience in investment banking, private equity, strategic finance, business operations, or a related analytical field, including 4+ years of strategic finance experience with systems, automation, or corporate finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience managing and developing ICs, with demonstrated success building and leading high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in financial planning, modeling, and creating data-driven analysis to partner with executive leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to distill complex issues into structured frameworks, build processes from scratch, and develop concrete action plans, with a process-oriented, automation-first mindset and initiative to learn and apply new technology and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of building relationships, communicating with stakeholders across all levels, and delivering compelling presentations/memos to executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a high-growth B2B SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in corporate finance or a G&amp;amp;A business partnering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with financial planning tools (e.g., Pigment, Anaplan, Hyperion, Adaptive) or HRIS/Procure-to-Pay systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently retrieve and analyze data using SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
